      "text": "In the right triangle $ABC$, we have $AB = 16$ and $BC = 24$. Since $\\angle A = 90^\\circ$, $\\sin A$ represents the ratio of the length of the side opposite the $90^\\circ$ angle (the height) to the length of the hypotenuse (the side opposite to $\\angle A$ and between the other two sides).\n\nThis can be written as: \n$$\\sin A = \\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{16}{24}$$\n\nNotice that this simplifies to $\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nSo, the value of $\\sin A$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}$.",
